#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:1
#: f2909393a65a45ae8a6fbbdcb6c4ee5a
msgid "Comparing Organizations across Different Operating Environments"
msgstr "在不同运营环境之间比较组织"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:3
#: d606581ebf984b5ea1f32380fec256ce
msgid ""
"Suppose two hospitals use the same categories of labor, beds, and equipment "
"to provide the same categories of care. One can recruit from a large labor "
"market, refer difficult cases to nearby specialists, and rely on mature "
"transport and digital infrastructure. The other serves a remote population, "
"has limited referral capacity, and faces persistent staffing constraints. "
"The hospitals share a mission, but they may not face the same production "
"opportunities."
msgstr "假设两家医院使用相同类别的员工、床位和设备，提供相同类别的医疗服务。其中一家可以从大型劳动力市场招聘，把疑难病例转诊给附近的专科机构，并依托成熟的交通与数字基础设施；另一家服务偏远地区人口，转诊能力有限，而且长期面临人员约束。两家医院使命相同，却未必面对相同的生产机会。"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:11
#: 6c30da3d781f41cc8c24d51dc4d2b33b
msgid ""
"A single comparison can then be misleading in either direction. Benchmarking"
" each hospital only against nearby peers respects its operating environment,"
" but conceals how far that environment lies from the strongest opportunities"
" observed elsewhere. Benchmarking every hospital against one common frontier"
" creates comparability, but risks presenting an opportunity disadvantage as "
"poor local performance."
msgstr "此时，只采用一种比较标准可能在两个方向上产生误导。只把每家医院与邻近同类机构比较，尊重了它的运营环境，却掩盖了该环境与其他地区所观察到的最强生产机会相距多远。把所有医院放到一条共同前沿上比较，建立了可比性，却可能把机会劣势误写成当地运营绩效不佳。"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:18
#: 492e06c8441f4c3a84a9fb225c86ff75
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Metafrontier analysis retains both standards. The within-group comparison "
"asks how well an organization uses the opportunities available under its own"
" infrastructure, mandate, or production system. The broader comparison then "
"asks how those locally available opportunities compare with the strongest "
"possibilities observed across all groups. Developed for firms operating "
"under different technologies or production environments, the decomposition "
"separates an organization's operating shortfall from an opportunity "
"disadvantage associated with its group {cite:p}`odonnell2008`."
msgstr ""
"共同前沿（metafrontier，亦称元前沿）分析同时保留两种标准。群组内比较考察组织在自身基础设施、职责任务或生产系统所提供的机会下，利用这些机会的表现如何；更广泛的比较则考察当地可用机会与全部群组中观察到的最强机会相距多远。这一分解最初用于面对不同生产技术或生产环境的企业，将组织自身的运营不足与其所在群组对应的机会劣势区分开来"
" {cite:p}`odonnell2008`。"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:27
#: 9461a857b99b46899b96962e3aec09e9
msgid ""
"This is useful whenever groups have an economic meaning established before "
"estimation: countries with different infrastructures, hospitals with "
"different service mandates, farms using different production systems, or "
"plants subject to different regulatory regimes. A group is not simply a "
"cluster that happened to emerge from the efficiency results. If group labels"
" are chosen after examining the scores, the decomposition becomes an "
"explanation constructed from the outcome it is meant to explain."
msgstr "只要群组在估计之前已有明确经济含义，这种分析就有价值，例如基础设施不同的国家、服务职责不同的医院、采用不同生产系统的农场，或面对不同监管制度的工厂。群组不能只是效率结果出来后碰巧形成的聚类。如果分析者看过效率值后才选择群组标签，分解就会变成由待解释结果反向构造的解释。"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:35
#: 7a1264bd883343d09203a8dad6c6dd72
msgid "Known groups are not discovered groups"
msgstr "已知群组不是模型发现的群组"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:38
#: 2ab115e17bd049bd8eb703fcc09c27ab
msgid ""
"This chapter begins with an institutional classification fixed before the "
"frontiers are estimated. Clustering instead asks the data to discover "
"groups; a conditional frontier asks how represented opportunities vary with "
"observed operating circumstances, which may be continuous. Those designs "
"require their own estimators and uncertainty accounts. The radial "
"metafrontier used here does neither: it compares the declared groups without"
" choosing, relabeling, or statistically conditioning them."
msgstr "本章从估计生产前沿之前已经确定的制度分类出发。聚类分析让数据发现群组；条件前沿则考察已表示的生产机会如何随实际观察到且可能连续变化的运营条件而变化。这些研究设计需要各自的估计方法与不确定性账户。这里采用的径向共同前沿方法两者都不做：它比较事先声明的群组，不替模型选择群组、重新贴标签或进行统计条件化。"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:47
#: 2691d955045a466da0e6264615782de0
msgid "Two standards answer two different questions"
msgstr "两种标准回答两个不同问题"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:49
#: 45ca1ca44e234e5fb616eef4e0c3a6d1
msgid "For an organization $o$ belonging to group $\\kappa$, the analysis asks:"
msgstr "对于属于群组 $\\kappa$ 的组织 $o$，分析提出两个问题："

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:51
#: 1b027bbc46774cde956f6e7b38cdf881
msgid ""
"**How well does the organization perform relative to attainable practice "
"represented within its own group?**"
msgstr "**相对于本群组所表示的可达到实践，该组织表现如何？**"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:53
#: 2aa10ef01ce9483ca2ad430eb510a1bf
msgid ""
"**How close is that group's frontier to the broader opportunity frontier "
"represented across all groups?**"
msgstr "**该群组的前沿与所有群组共同表示的更广泛机会前沿有多接近？**"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:56
#: 0cc3498e712e48a9ba63236910074b4d
msgid ""
"The first question yields **group efficiency**, denoted $E_o^G$. The same "
"organization is then evaluated against the metafrontier, yielding **meta "
"efficiency**, $E_o^M$. Their ratio is the **metatechnology ratio**:"
msgstr ""
"第一个问题得到**群组效率**，记作 $E_o^G$。然后把同一组织放到共同前沿下评价，得到**共同前沿效率** "
"$E_o^M$。二者之比是**共同技术比率（MTR）**："

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:60
#: 489a648a8d184561978dfe584049daf9
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"MTR_o=\\frac{E_o^M}{E_o^G}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"MTR_o=\\frac{E_o^M}{E_o^G}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:64
#: 5e743f8c1b1d4479ba45f3e77768dad6
msgid ""
"The literature also calls this the *technology gap ratio* (TGR). A value "
"nearer one means that the best practice available within the group "
"approaches the broader best practice observed for the organization's "
"resource and service mix. A lower value signals a larger opportunity gap at "
"that mix. It does not say that local managers caused the gap or could remove"
" infrastructure, regulatory, or mandate differences on their own."
msgstr "文献也把它称为*技术差距比*（TGR）。数值越接近一，表示对于该组织的资源与服务组合，群组内可达到的最佳实践越接近更广泛范围内观察到的最佳实践；数值越低，表示该组合下的机会差距越大。它并不表明当地管理者造成了这一差距，也不意味着他们能够凭自身力量消除基础设施、监管或职责任务差异。"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:71
#: 8ddc128fdcd24765bf6bd136527ca7aa
msgid "The three quantities obey the accounting identity"
msgstr "三个量满足如下核算恒等式："

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:73
#: 0c648409e462450a87570dfc30295520
msgid ""
"\n"
"E_o^M=E_o^G\\times MTR_o.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"E_o^M=E_o^G\\times MTR_o.\n"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:77
#: e07838b5886847d79e0ca531fd8fc662
msgid ""
"Consider an organization that uses four units of a resource and delivers two"
" units of service. At this resource commitment, its group frontier supports "
"four services, while the metafrontier supports eight. Its group efficiency "
"is $2/4=0.50$, its meta efficiency is $2/8=0.25$, and its MTR is $4/8=0.50$."
msgstr ""
"考察一个使用四单位资源、提供两单位服务的组织。在这一资源承诺下，其群组前沿可以支持四单位服务，共同前沿可以支持八单位服务。因此，群组效率为 "
"$2/4=0.50$，共同前沿效率为 $2/8=0.25$，MTR 为 $4/8=0.50$。"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:82
#: ee4a3041de394dfb97e0b9ca1a0ddc96
msgid ""
"An organization using four resource units delivers two services, while its "
"group frontier supports four and the pooled metafrontier supports eight; "
"group efficiency is one half, the metatechnology ratio is one half, and meta"
" efficiency is one quarter"
msgstr "一个组织使用四单位资源提供两单位服务，而群组前沿可支持四单位服务、合并共同前沿可支持八单位服务；群组效率为二分之一，共同技术比率为二分之一，共同前沿效率为四分之一"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:87
#: 537ef84b0ae14e2fba9d9d06994a9a91
msgid ""
"The same observed operation is assessed against two opportunity standards. "
"The decomposition distinguishes performance within the declared group from "
"the proximity of that group's frontier to the broader meta opportunity."
msgstr "同一项实际运营接受两种机会标准的评价。该分解把事先声明群组内的运营绩效，与群组前沿接近更广泛共同机会的程度区分开来。"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:92
#: f315654ae513448aa3a9f62b4e0f314c
msgid ""
"The distinction changes the conversation. A process-redesign or maintenance "
"programme may be relevant when an organization lies behind its group "
"frontier. Infrastructure investment, regulatory reform, access to capital, "
"or a change in service mandate may be relevant when the group frontier lies "
"behind the meta opportunity. The scores organize these questions; they do "
"not show that any named intervention will cause an improvement."
msgstr "这种区分会改变管理讨论的重点。当组织落后于群组前沿时，过程再设计或维护计划可能值得关注；当群组前沿落后于共同机会时，基础设施投资、监管改革、资本可得性或服务职责调整可能更为相关。这些效率值有助于梳理这些问题，却不能证明任何一项具体干预必然带来改善。"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:99
#: 3525dfb8984e48f9a86723a8291717b2
msgid "The radial metafrontier account"
msgstr "径向共同前沿账户"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:101
#: a2f55816c9fd4c53a9e03e3e29690854
msgid ""
"Let organization $o$ use input vector $x_o$ to deliver desirable-output "
"vector $y_o$. Its declared group is $\\kappa$. The matrices $X_\\kappa$ and "
"$Y_\\kappa$ contain the eligible observations in that group, while $X_M$ and"
" $Y_M$ contain eligible observations from all declared groups. The "
"variables, measurement units, mission boundary, orientation, returns to "
"scale, and time information must be the same in the two comparisons. Only "
"the reference population changes."
msgstr ""
"令组织 $o$ 使用投入向量 $x_o$ 提供合意产出向量 $y_o$，其事先声明的群组为 $\\kappa$。矩阵 $X_\\kappa$ 与 "
"$Y_\\kappa$ 包含该群组内的合格观测，$X_M$ 与 $Y_M$ "
"则包含所有已声明群组的合格观测。两次比较必须采用相同的变量、计量单位、使命边界、导向、规模报酬和时期信息；改变的只有参照总体。"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:109
#: 9cb4c4f75f8e4eb089bc7369976d4640
msgid ""
"For an output-oriented analysis under variable returns to scale, the group "
"programme is"
msgstr "在规模报酬可变的产出导向分析中，群组规划为"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:112
#: c9f9a8e971204e1786b5249205931ab3
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\phi_o^G=\\max_{\\phi,\\lambda}\\quad &\\phi\\\\\n"
"\\text{subject to}\\quad\n"
"&X_\\kappa\\lambda\\leq x_o,\\\\\n"
"&Y_\\kappa\\lambda\\geq\\phi y_o,\\\\\n"
"&\\mathbf 1^\\top\\lambda=1,\\qquad \\lambda\\geq0.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\phi_o^G=\\max_{\\phi,\\lambda}\\quad &\\phi\\\\\n"
"\\text{约束条件}\\quad\n"
"&X_\\kappa\\lambda\\leq x_o,\\\\\n"
"&Y_\\kappa\\lambda\\geq\\phi y_o,\\\\\n"
"&\\mathbf 1^\\top\\lambda=1,\\qquad \\lambda\\geq0.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:122
#: 977bee1b389d4edfbc9bc740c99f6740
msgid ""
"The expansion factor $\\phi_o^G$ asks how much all recorded outputs could be"
" increased together while inputs remain fixed. Reporting $E_o^G=1/\\phi_o^G$"
" places group efficiency on the familiar higher-is-better scale from zero to"
" one. The meta programme has the same form but replaces the group matrices "
"with the pooled matrices:"
msgstr ""
"扩张因子 $\\phi_o^G$ 考察在投入保持不变时，所有记录产出可以同比例增加多少。报告 "
"$E_o^G=1/\\phi_o^G$，就把群组效率置于熟悉的零到一且数值越高越好的尺度上。共同前沿规划形式相同，只把群组矩阵替换为合并矩阵："

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:128
#: 0c7403f5ff034346a368cebd1c0c226c
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\phi_o^M=\\max_{\\phi,\\lambda}\\quad &\\phi\\\\\n"
"\\text{subject to}\\quad\n"
"&X_M\\lambda\\leq x_o,\\\\\n"
"&Y_M\\lambda\\geq\\phi y_o,\\\\\n"
"&\\mathbf 1^\\top\\lambda=1,\\qquad \\lambda\\geq0.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\phi_o^M=\\max_{\\phi,\\lambda}\\quad &\\phi\\\\\n"
"\\text{约束条件}\\quad\n"
"&X_M\\lambda\\leq x_o,\\\\\n"
"&Y_M\\lambda\\geq\\phi y_o,\\\\\n"
"&\\mathbf 1^\\top\\lambda=1,\\qquad \\lambda\\geq0.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:138
#: a35eff5372694214bdd4cac930088e95
msgid "Thus $E_o^M=1/\\phi_o^M$ and"
msgstr "因此 $E_o^M=1/\\phi_o^M$，且"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:140
#: 134261897a234b9fb92a3a5c68aaac3c
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"MTR_o=\\frac{E_o^M}{E_o^G}\n"
"     =\\frac{\\phi_o^G}{\\phi_o^M}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"MTR_o=\\frac{E_o^M}{E_o^G}\n"
"     =\\frac{\\phi_o^G}{\\phi_o^M}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:145
#: 39501139efec41abb445d23817db5e99
msgid ""
"Because the pooled comparison population contains the organization's own "
"group, it cannot offer fewer represented opportunities than the matched "
"group comparison. With valid nested technologies,"
msgstr "由于合并比较总体包含该组织自己的群组，它所表示的生产机会不可能少于口径匹配的群组比较。在有效嵌套的生产技术下，"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:149
#: b29791b370824c4a873d9bd25fc56dc5
msgid ""
"\n"
"0<E_o^M\\leq E_o^G\\leq1,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"0<MTR_o\\leq1.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"0<E_o^M\\leq E_o^G\\leq1,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"0<MTR_o\\leq1.\n"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:155
#: 7a8712504ee840fdb31becece8ced6f4
msgid ""
"An input-oriented analysis protects the observed output commitments and asks"
" how far inputs could contract. If $\\theta_o^G$ and $\\theta_o^M$ are the "
"corresponding input efficiencies, then"
msgstr "投入导向分析保护实际产出承诺，并考察投入可以收缩多少。若 $\\theta_o^G$ 与 $\\theta_o^M$ 是相应的投入效率，则"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:159
#: aba0cdc6f2134c569fb736ee194855d9
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"MTR_o=\\frac{\\theta_o^M}{\\theta_o^G}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"MTR_o=\\frac{\\theta_o^M}{\\theta_o^G}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:163
#: 98a121cb162840898669c6d679f4a466
msgid ""
"The orientation should follow the organization's decision problem. An output"
" orientation may suit a hospital expected to serve more patients with a "
"largely fixed estate; an input orientation may suit a programme required to "
"deliver a fixed service obligation at lower resource cost. Under constant "
"returns to scale, matched input- and output-oriented radial efficiencies "
"coincide. Under variable returns to scale they need not, so orientation is "
"not a harmless presentational choice."
msgstr "导向应服从组织的决策问题。对于主要资产大致固定、但被要求服务更多患者的医院，产出导向可能合适；对于必须以更低资源成本完成固定服务义务的项目，投入导向可能合适。在规模报酬不变下，口径匹配的投入导向与产出导向径向效率相同；在规模报酬可变下则未必如此，因此导向不是无关紧要的展示选择。"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:171
#: 46ebaef36c194565a9c12c7f0acfbc18
msgid ""
"The scale assumption also has substantive content. Variable returns to scale"
" compares an organization with convex combinations at a comparable scale. "
"Constant returns to scale admits proportional replication of observed "
"activities. A study should choose between them from its account of the "
"sector, not from whichever version produces a preferred ranking."
msgstr "规模假设同样具有实质含义。规模报酬可变把组织与相近规模活动的凸组合比较；规模报酬不变允许把实际观察活动按比例复制。研究应根据对行业生产过程的理解选择二者，而不是选择能够产生偏好排名的版本。"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:177
#: ec09c42630c94010989e82d282db7e38
msgid "A pooled frontier is not merely a union of group frontiers"
msgstr "合并前沿并非只是各群组前沿的并集"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:179
#: 1ee20a4fc02549cfa72bbf8c6c059dad
msgid ""
"There are two ideas that are easy to confuse. At the conceptual level, the "
"meta opportunity can be described as the union of the opportunities "
"available to the separate groups. Such a union need not be convex: an "
"activity feasible under one institutional regime and another activity "
"feasible under a different regime do not automatically imply that every "
"mixture of the two is feasible."
msgstr "这里有两个容易混淆的概念。在理论层面，共同机会可以描述为各群组分别可用机会的并集。这样的并集未必是凸的：某项活动在一种制度下可行，另一项活动在另一种制度下可行，并不自动意味着二者的每一种混合方案都可行。"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:186
#: d971ee9c8c39416a8fdb23a147a50224
msgid ""
"The radial DEA estimator used here instead pools all eligible observations "
"and, under VRS, takes their common convex hull. It can therefore construct a"
" meta benchmark by combining observations from different groups. A rural "
"hospital and an urban hospital, for example, may jointly define a virtual "
"comparator even though no real institution has exactly that configuration. "
"Under CRS the analogous pooled technology is conic rather than convex."
msgstr ""
"这里使用的径向 DEA 估计量则合并所有合格观测，并在 VRS "
"下取它们的共同凸包。因此，它可以通过组合不同群组的观测来构造共同前沿标杆。例如，一家乡村医院与一家城市医院可能共同界定一个虚拟比较对象，即使现实中没有任何机构恰好具有这种配置。在"
" CRS 下，对应的合并生产技术是锥包，而不是凸包。"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:193
#: 4bcc76bc51b6405cb815f4e69f66f65d
msgid ""
"This distinction matters because the pooled hull is generally at least as "
"expansive as the nonconvex union of separately estimated group hulls. It can"
" therefore produce a lower meta efficiency and MTR. That is not a "
"computational quirk; it follows from the maintained assumption that cross-"
"group mixtures describe relevant opportunities. The assumption may be "
"defensible when groups differ in degree but share transferable practices. It"
" is harder to defend when regulations, production systems, or missions make "
"the mixed plan institutionally impossible."
msgstr ""
"这一区别很重要，因为合并凸包通常至少与分别估计的群组凸包之非凸并集一样宽广，因而可能产生更低的共同前沿效率和 "
"MTR。这不是计算异常，而是来自一项既定假设：跨群组混合方案代表相关生产机会。当群组只是程度不同且实践可以转移时，该假设可能站得住脚；当监管、生产系统或使命使混合方案在制度上不可能实施时，它就较难成立。"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:202
#: f27de0fd318f4a9c868ba844f5fe7496
msgid ""
"Accordingly, the MTR is always conditional on how the meta opportunity has "
"been constructed. Researchers should examine which groups contribute to "
"important meta benchmarks and explain whether the associated practices can "
"be combined, transferred, or approached. A meta target may describe a useful"
" long-run opportunity without being an immediately adoptable operating plan."
msgstr ""
"因此，MTR "
"始终取决于共同机会的构造方式。研究者应检查哪些群组为重要的共同前沿标杆作出贡献，并说明相关实践能否组合、转移或逐步接近。共同前沿目标可以描述有价值的长期机会，却未必是一套可立即采用的运营方案。"

#: ../../chapters/07-heterogeneity/23-metafrontier.md:208
#: c6a100964f8f4321be0bf982a3fbba2d
msgid "A six-organization laboratory"
msgstr "一个包含六个组织的实验案例"

